-- #6522 sandbox fixture: DesignFlow sandbox (xupnyeifmpsacrqahwwm) ONLY. Never apply to shared preview or production.
-- designflow-backend#408 step 5 live proof: seeds the exact production fixture
-- closure for two SKUs so plm.suggested_property_for_sku can render the Item
-- Detail suggestion UI on alsand in both states:
--   BG12VDYCP01  art = Aristocats (4 files)   current MG06 = CP Classic Characters  -> mismatch warning
--   3FZ27DYNX01  art = Nightmare (1 file)     current MG06 = NX Nightmare           -> agreeing hint
-- Rows are ported from a read-only production extract (2026-11-16). One
-- deliberate divergence: plm.dcp_crawl rows stay status 'running' (production
-- had crawl 49c393e7 complete) because the repo-wide source_capture_inventory
-- contract requires "No complete DCP crawl exists" on a freshly migrated
-- database, and nothing in the suggestion feature reads crawl status. The
-- metadata runs finalize to 'complete' exactly as production recorded.
-- Cross-boundary FK columns are NULLed (dcp_property.core_property_id and
-- metadata-run references, dcp_style_guide.core_style_guide_id and crawl
-- references, dcp_crawl.baseline_*), so the fixture never references anything
-- outside itself. Idempotent: every insert is on conflict do nothing.
-- Reversal: delete these rows by the ids below (fixture ids are stable).
--
-- DECLARED DEPENDENCY (review finding #6534): this fixture seeds DATA only.
-- The structure it reads -- plm.suggested_property_for_sku and
-- plm.dcp_property_mg06_crosswalk (16 films, incl. ar/aristocats -> AC and
-- ti/tim-burton-s-nightmare-before-christmas -> NX) -- comes from migrations
-- 20261115132055 and 20261116120000, which the DesignFlow sandbox has already
-- applied (sandbox ledger, verified 2026-11-16). It is deliberately not
-- re-seeded here; the guard below fails loudly if it is ever missing.
--
-- Fidelity notes (review finding #6534): coldlion.item_detail has rows only
-- for 3FZ27DYNX01 (4); BG12VDYCP01 genuinely has NO item_detail rows and its
-- item_merch_group rows are header-scope (item_pkey IS NULL) with slot 9
-- absent -- that is exactly what production holds, not an omission.
-- derived-from: none

-- Guard: the two structure migrations this fixture depends on must be present.
do $dep$
begin
  if not exists (
    select 1 from pg_proc
    where proname = 'suggested_property_for_sku'
      and pronamespace = 'plm'::regnamespace
  ) or (select count(*) from plm.dcp_property_mg06_crosswalk) < 16 then
    raise exception using errcode = 'P0001',
      message = 'sandbox fixture 20261202130000: plm migrations 20261115132055/20261116120000 (suggested_property_for_sku + crosswalk) must be applied first';
  end if;
end
$dep$;
